docs/playwright-interop.md:3:> **Naming clarification.** "Playwright CLI" in this repo means [`@playwright/cli`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@playwright/cli) — the imperative shell binary `playwright-cli` that exposes commands like `attach`, `snapshot`, `click`, and `eval`. It is **not** the same as [`@playwright/test`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@playwright/test), which is the spec runner invoked as `npx playwright test`. Both work with dap-cli; the imperative `playwright-cli` is the primary inspiration for dap-cli's command surface and the recommended interop driver for hand-driven and agent-driven workflows.
