Usage: dap-cli attach [options]

Start a DAP attach session using an adapter id, named launch config, or fake
adapter

Options:
  --adapter <adapter>                 adapter id (inferred from --type or
                                      --program when omitted)
  --config <name>                     named .vscode/launch.json configuration
  --workspace <path>                  workspace root for .vscode/launch.json
                                      discovery and variable substitution
  --list-configs                      list VS Code launch configurations and
                                      compounds without starting a session
  --json <json>                       raw adapter-native attach configuration
                                      JSON (default: "{}")
  --script <script>                   fake adapter script
  --name <name>                       session name (default: "default")
  --program <path>                    program path override
  --cwd <path>                        working directory override
  --runtime-executable <path>         runtime executable override
  --runtime-args <arg...>             runtime argument overrides
  --url <url>                         URL override for browser adapters
  --port <port>                       debug port override
  --python <path>                     Python executable override
  --type <type>                       adapter-native debug type (inferred from
                                      --adapter or --program when omitted)
  --args <arg...>                     program argument overrides
  --source-maps <boolean>             source map enablement override
  --out-files <pattern...>            source map output file patterns
  --resolve-source-maps <pattern...>  set resolveSourceMapLocations on the
                                      resolved config (variadic; mirrors
                                      --out-files)
  --json-overrides <json>             extra JSON object merged on top of
                                      --config (between named-config and --json
                                      layers)
  --stop-on-entry                     halt at the first program statement
                                      (adapter must support stopOnEntry)
  --no-use                            do not make the new session active
  -h, --help                          display help for command
Usage: dap-cli pause [options]

Pause execution (auto-resolves to the unique thread if --thread-id omitted)

Options:
